{"duration_api_ms":204119,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b0f667f5-a846-4cbc-a94f-3d6608a375c6","total_cost_usd":0.235062,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12992,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18309,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12992,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18309,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12992},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18309,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12992,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.235062,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":13162,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is 3 points clustered at D~3.34, B=1.2, cone=69.5, gamma -2.8 to -3.5, with normalised HV 0.347. Fitting the near-front rows gives limits set by three constraints. Peak g is about 12 (margin 0.01 at 11.879), and it depends mainly on gamma, rising about 1.64 g/deg, with a weak D effect of about +0.375 g/m. Heatshield mass-fraction margin falls linearly with D at about 0.58 per m, reaching zero near D~3.385 at B=1.2, cone=69.5. Bondline temperature is far below its 450 K limit. Flux and temperature improve slightly with larger D, and the (B=1.2, cone=69.5) corner is the best of the points tested. The g limit puts the steep end near gamma ~ -3.57 at D 3.38. Shallower gamma lowers flux and raises T (about 24 kW/m2 and 11 K per deg). 17 of 60 evaluations returned no geometry. Failures are either a cone angle too small for the bluntness (B=1.2 with cone 66) or cd_fore hull extrapolation at cone 69-70 with B=1.25, or at D 3.0 to 2.8. I therefore stay near the known-good (B, cone) corner and make only three small probes.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-8809880a095e (D3.38, gamma -3.5) has lower flux (273.5k) and lower T (391.86 K) than C-37807858716a (D3.34: 278.3k, 392.57 K). Larger D helps on both objectives, and its mass margin is only 0.0029.\",\"Mass margin vs D at B=1.2, cone=69.5: 3.2 -> 0.1063, 3.3 -> 0.0496, 3.34 -> 0.0264, 3.36 -> 0.0147, 3.38 -> 0.0029. This gives a linear extrapolation to zero at D~3.385.\",\"g at gamma -3.5, B=1.2, cone=69.5: 11.849 (D3.3), 11.864 (D3.34), 11.879 (D3.38). g vs gamma: -2.8 -> 10.769, -3.2 -> 11.379, -3.5 -> 11.864, -3.8 -> 12.309 (C-94a9f7a46f9b, infeasible). C-dc8f61b27df5 (D3.2, gamma -3.59) has g 11.957 and is feasible.\",\"C-681765084fb2 (gamma -2.8) has 261k / 400.2 K, C-eabe3605e502 (gamma -3.2) has 270.9k / 395.7 K. Shallower gamma trades higher T for lower flux, so the front can be extended toward gamma -1.5.\",\"C-f84c59a3cc23 (gamma -5.54) reaches T=378.9 K but g=15.6, so steeper entry is unreachable under the g limit.\",\"Failures: C-40f2342796ee (D3.0, B1.2, cone 69), C-5b57439845df (B1.25, cone 70) and C-4b1b4e110042 (B1.25, cone 70) are hull-extrapolation failures. C-3cd51d4bc9fc (B1.2, cone 66) is an invalid geometry. Successful corner points are (1.2, 69.5), (1.15, 68.5), (1.1, 67) and (0.95, 69.5).\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g depends mostly on entry angle, so it is nearly geometry-independent. The g limit therefore caps gamma near -3.57, and the mass fraction caps D near 3.385. Within those caps, larger D lowers ballistic coefficient, so flux and T fall. A larger nose radius (higher B) and a larger cone angle also lower flux and T slightly. The best design is at the corner D~3.38, B=1.2, cone~69.5, gamma just shallower than -3.57. Moving to that corner at each gamma should dominate the D3.34 front points. Shallower gamma at D=3.38 adds coverage of the low-flux, higher-T end. This is fitted from the data; the extrapolation to gamma of about -1.6 relies on smooth trends and is less certain.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The gamma-to-g edge is within about 0.01 g of the limit, so the -3.56 and -3.57 points may violate max_g. The mass margin at D=3.384 is about 0.0006, which is also marginal. The T(gamma) curve beyond gamma -2.8 is extrapolated and may be more convex than assumed. The B/cone probes (B 1.22, cone 70, cone 69.8) may hit cd_fore hull extrapolation failures, since the hull shape near the corner is unknown and (1.2, 69) failed at D3.0.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Push toward the g limit at the maximum feasible D to lower T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the steep edge of the front where g margin is about 0.002.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly steeper than the current best, with a safer g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-8809880a095e with a small T gain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Use the last bit of mass margin (zero near D 3.385) for a small flux and T gain.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction boundary precisely; the margin is only about 0.0006.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the front at D3.38 slightly shallower than -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Dominates existing D3.34 points at nearby gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at gamma -3.4 with D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolation between the known front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Front coverage at gamma -3.3 with D=3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Larger-D version of the C-eabe3605e502 region; should dominate it.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Same gamma as C-eabe3605e502 with larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":266300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct test of the D 3.34 to 3.38 gain on a known front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front coverage at gamma -3.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between -3.2 and -2.8.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front coverage at gamma -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between -3.2 and -2.8.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Larger-D version of front point C-681765084fb2 (gamma -2.8).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Should dominate C-681765084fb2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front to lower flux with shallower entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the extrapolated trend in the low-flux, higher-T direction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Extend the front further toward low flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front beyond the current shallowest point (gamma -2.8).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Continue extending the shallow end.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the T(gamma) curve is convex.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-end coverage at gamma -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front and probes the T penalty of shallow entry.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-end coverage at gamma -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shallow-end coverage of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Test the shallowest extreme of the gamma range.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the extrapolated trend near the gamma bound; long-duration heating may curve T upward faster.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-77d44f39be75\",\"rationale\":\"Steeper gamma at D3.36, which has a larger mass margin (0.0147) than D3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the edge of the g limit at a slightly smaller D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly higher B at the same cone angle. Higher B lowers flux and T and adds mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the surrogate hull boundary beyond B=1.2; it may fail the extrapolation check.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Cone angle at the upper bound, B=1.2. Larger cone gives higher drag and more mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the hull near cone=70; C-5b57439845df (B1.25, cone 70) failed, but B=1.2 may be inside.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8809880a095e\",\"rationale\":\"Small cone increase from 69.5 to 69.8, a lower-risk probe of the same direction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives a gradient in cone angle at the best corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":161848,"type":"result","duration_ms":204164,"uuid":"59228206-926d-4f74-a3cb-b79e29118d36","ttft_stream_ms":1638,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":1638,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
